  "notes": [
    "N1/N2 use a 240x160 generalized navigation engine in src/core/game-navigation.ts behind game.dispatch; spec/navigation and the original 40x20 exports/tests are unchanged.",
    "Navigation states are constructed and driven through game.scenario and game.dispatch, not private state casts.",
    "V1 uses the pure 12x20 presentation camera in src/web/camera.ts; browser tests check DPR backing, visible cells, clamping and resize against the real core state.",
    "B1/B2 share one pure game.build empty->well/ring transition; the keyboard menu also uses it and game.preview composes the real target-patch glyphs without mutating the world.",
    "Build menus preserve pendingSource; blocked keys are identity and blur or Escape cancellation never constructs.",
    "I2/L1/L2 use one pure game.link transition; Insert drafts are bounded to 32 printable characters, keyboard commit/retry/cancel and direct link events share that transition, and browser arrows are presentation overlays over the composed text field.",
    "E1-E4/T1-T2 use one private economy/tick transition behind game.advance and the elapsed/visibility events; generation, ascending-well transfer, ordered ring summoning, saturated buffers and pause/suspension are checked against the shared corpus plus independent property examples."
